## Supe — Multiverse Orchestration Engine

Supe explores multiple solution approaches simultaneously. Define a problem, and Supe runs N isolated universes in parallel — each with a different strategy — then cross-pollinates insights between them.

### When to Use

- You want to compare fundamentally different approaches to the same problem
- You're unsure which architecture, framework, or strategy is best
- You want parallel exploration with automatic insight sharing

### Usage

```bash
# Explore approaches for a new feature on this project
supe run --spec <path-to-spec.md> --base-repo . --universes 3

# Start fresh (no base project)
supe run --spec <path-to-spec.md> --universes 3
```

### Key Options

| Option | Description | Default |
|--------|-------------|---------|
| `--spec <path>` | Problem specification file (required) | — |
| `--base-repo <path>` | Existing project to use as base | none (empty dir) |
| `--universes <n>` | Number of parallel universes | 3 |
| `--agent <type>` | Agent type (`claude` or `codex`) | claude |
| `--no-pollen` | Disable cross-pollination | enabled |

### Output

Results are stored in `~/.supe/sessions/`. Use these commands to inspect:

```bash
supe status          # Current session status
supe report          # Comparison report across universes
supe list            # All sessions
```
